EF AI Workspace (#243): the chat keeps its centred reading column on every screen, as ChatGPT and Claude do.

- Settings (Nav/Settings/registry.tsx): no «تكبير مساحة الدردشة» (Maximize chat space). Turned on in a desktop browser,
  it dropped the 48rem reading width (brand.css UX-11): one long line per reply, a screen-wide message box, and the
  model name far from the reply. ChatGPT (about 48rem) and Claude keep a centred column with no full-width option.
- store/settings.ts: maximizeChatSpace is a plain atom, false, no longer read from localStorage, so a browser that
  saved «maximize» gets the centred column back without doing anything. Its readers stay as upstream.
  - store/__tests__/maximizeChatSpace.spec.ts: a saved «maximize» is ignored; Settings does not offer it.

